<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1999</h1><p class="ref-lede">1999 in world history: 10 events, 13 deaths and 1 state that came to an end. 188 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1995">1995</a><a href="/years/1996">1996</a><a href="/years/1997">1997</a><a href="/years/1998">1998</a><a href="/years/1999" aria-current="page">1999</a><a href="/years/2000">2000</a><a href="/years/2001">2001</a><a href="/years/2002">2002</a><a href="/years/2003">2003</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-1">1 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The euro is launched in eleven European countries</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The euro became the official currency of eleven EU states, used at first for electronic transactions and financial markets. National notes and coins remained in circulation for three more years.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-20">20 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Two students kill 13 people at Columbine High School</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Two students at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colorado">Colorado</a> school shot dead twelve classmates and a teacher before killing themselves. The attack transformed school security and police response tactics across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-29">29 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Nigeria returns to civilian rule</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Olusegun Obasanjo was sworn in as president, ending fifteen years of military government. The date was kept as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>'s Democracy Day until 2019, when it moved to 12 June.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-30">30 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">East Timor votes for independence</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In a UN-run referendum, 78.5 per cent of East Timorese voted for independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>. Militia violence followed until an Australian-led force restored order; independence came in 2002.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-timor">East Timor</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-31">31 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Boris Yeltsin resigns and hands power to Vladimir Putin</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In a New Year's Eve television address, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boris-yeltsin">Boris Yeltsin</a> unexpectedly resigned as president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. Prime Minister Vladimir Putin became acting president and won election in March 2000.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">War</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/kargil-war">Kargil War</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Kargil War was an armed conflict between India and Pakistan from May to July 1999 in the Kargil district, then part of the state of Jammu and Kashmir.</p></div></li></ol></section>
